     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "ReviewBoard requires a local copy of the repository to work...so I set up a cron job to pull from github every 30 mins.  Looks like it works...here's an example review, where I posted the diff of the most recent commit to the repo: ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://review.duraspace.org/r/23/"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://review.duraspace.org/r/23/",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This functions, but it's probably worth considering, if we move to github, whether to just use its built-in code review capability.  It looks pretty nice, and doesn't require people to generate diffs...",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
