     },
     "body": "<p>ReviewBoard requires a local copy of the repository to work...so I set up a cron job to pull from github every 30 mins.  Looks like it works...here's an example review, where I posted the diff of the most recent commit to the repo: <a href=\"https://review.duraspace.org/r/23/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://review.duraspace.org/r/23/</a></p>\n\n<p>This functions, but it's probably worth considering, if we move to github, whether to just use its built-in code review capability.  It looks pretty nice, and doesn't require people to generate diffs...</p>",
     "created": "12/Nov/10 9:42 PM",
     "id": "11682",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10768/comment/11682",
